# sambuca :: line-ending policy
#
# EVERY text file in this repository is LF, unconditionally.
#
# This is not a style preference. The engine ships shell scripts that run as the
# init path of a headless appliance, and a CRLF line ending there is not a
# cosmetic problem — `#!/bin/sh\r` is not a valid interpreter, and `then\r` is
# not `then`. dash rejects the file outright; bash sometimes tolerates it, which
# is worse, because the breakage then only appears on the target machine.
#
# It has already happened once in this repo's history: an editing pass on
# Windows rewrote 19 files to CRLF, and dash refused the installer's abort
# countdown — the one script whose job is to stop an unattended disk wipe.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalises on commit AND checkout, so a contributor on
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true cannot reintroduce it.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where it is load-bearing.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.cfg       text eol=lf
*.env       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
preseed.cfg text eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.iso    binary
*.bundle binary
